        { ar: 'ST-4 أصلاً Must — ما منعها من العدّ هو الصلاحية وحدها، لا الأولوية.', en: 'ST-4 is already Must — what kept it out of the tally was validity alone, not priority.' },
        { ar: 'بجملة so that تجتاز الفحص الثلاثي فتصير valid، فتدخل عدّ must مباشرة.', en: 'With a so-that clause it passes the three-part check, becomes valid, and enters the must tally directly.' },
        { ar: 'الصالحون صاروا أربعة، وثلاثتهم Must: ST-1 وST-2 وST-4.', en: 'The valid set becomes four, and three of them are Must: ST-1, ST-2 and ST-4.' },
        { ar: 'الجواب: 3', en: 'Answer: 3' },
      ],
    },
    {
      kind: 'debug',
      id: 'ex5.debug-loose-validator',
      required: true,
      brokenCode: "STORIES = [\n    {'key': 'ST-1', 'priority': 'Must', 'story': 'As a clerk, I want to flag a patient, so that the clinician prepares before the visit.'},\n    {'key': 'ST-2', 'priority': 'Must', 'story': 'As a clerk, I want to search by phone, so that I can fix misspelled records inline.'},\n    {'key': 'ST-3', 'priority': 'Should', 'story': 'As a manager, I want weekly no-show rates, so that staffing can be planned.'},\n    {'key': 'ST-4', 'priority': 'Must', 'story': 'As a clinician, I want faster charts.'},\n]\n\ndef valid_story(s):\n    # WRONG rule: checks the prefix and the want clause only\n    return s.startswith('As a') and 'I want' in s\n\npack = []\nfor st in STORIES:\n    ok = valid_story(st['story'])\n    pack.append((st['key'], st['priority'], ok))\n    print('%s %s %s' % (st['key'], st['priority'], 'valid' if ok else 'INVALID'))\nvalid = sum(1 for _, _, ok in pack if ok)\nmust = sum(1 for _, p, ok in pack if ok and p == 'Must')\nprint('stories: %d valid: %d must: %d' % (len(STORIES), valid, must))",
      prompt: {
        ar: 'الحزمة تطبع أرقامًا واثقة: ST-4 Must valid وحصيلة stories: 4 valid: 4 must: 3. لكن ST-4 بلا جملة so that أصلًا — لا لماذا، لا معيار قبول ممكن، لا محادثة — ومع ذلك دخلت عدّ الجاهزية! القاعدة المعيبة تفحص البادئة وكلمة I want فقط وتتغافل عن الجزء الأهم. أصلح valid_story إلى القاعدة الثلاثية (البادئة As a متباعدة عن الفاصلة، ثم , I want، ثم , so that) حتى تعود الحقيقة: ST-4 Must INVALID وحصيلة stories: 4 valid: 3 must: 2. واختبر دالتك على قصة صالحة وقصة بلا فائدة.',
        en: 'The pack prints confident numbers: ST-4 Must valid and a tally of stories: 4 valid: 4 must: 3. But ST-4 has no so-that clause at all — no why, no possible acceptance test, no conversation — yet it entered the readiness tally! The faulty rule checks only the prefix and the word I want, ignoring the most important part. Fix valid_story into the three-part rule (the spaced As a prefix, then , I want, then , so that) until the truth returns: ST-4 Must INVALID and a tally of stories: 4 valid: 3 must: 2. And test your function on a valid story and a benefit-less one.',
      },
      solution: "STORIES = [\n    {'key': 'ST-1', 'priority': 'Must', 'story': 'As a clerk, I want to flag a patient, so that the clinician prepares before the visit.'},\n    {'key': 'ST-2', 'priority': 'Must', 'story': 'As a clerk, I want to search by phone, so that I can fix misspelled records inline.'},\n    {'key': 'ST-3', 'priority': 'Should', 'story': 'As a manager, I want weekly no-show rates, so that staffing can be planned.'},\n    {'key': 'ST-4', 'priority': 'Must', 'story': 'As a clinician, I want faster charts.'},\n]\n\ndef valid_story(s):\n    return s.startswith('As a ') and ', I want ' in s and ', so that ' in s\n\npack = []\nfor st in STORIES:\n    ok = valid_story(st['story'])\n    pack.append((st['key'], st['priority'], ok))\n    print('%s %s %s' % (st['key'], st['priority'], 'valid' if ok else 'INVALID'))\nvalid = sum(1 for _, _, ok in pack if ok)\nmust = sum(1 for _, p, ok in pack if ok and p == 'Must')\nprint('stories: %d valid: %d must: %d' % (len(STORIES), valid, must))",
      tests: [
        {
          id: 't1',
          name: { ar: 'الحقيقة تعود للحصيلة', en: 'The truth returns to the tally' },
          code: "assert 'stories: 4 valid: 3 must: 2' in __learner_output__ and 'ST-4 Must INVALID' in __learner_output__, 'expected: stories: 4 valid: 3 must: 2 + ST-4 Must INVALID | actual: %r' % __learner_output__",
          expected: 'stories: 4 valid: 3 must: 2 + ST-4 Must INVALID',
        },
        {
          id: 't2',
          name: { ar: 'القاعدة الثلاثية تقبل الصالحة وترفض بلا فائدة', en: 'The three-part rule accepts the sound story and rejects the benefit-less one' },
          code: "assert valid_story('As a clerk, I want to flag a patient, so that the clinician prepares.') is True, 'expected: True | actual: %r' % valid_story('As a clerk, I want to flag a patient, so that the clinician prepares.')\nassert valid_story('As a clerk, I want to flag a patient.') is False, 'expected: False | actual: %r' % valid_story('As a clerk, I want to flag a patient.')",
          expected: 'True + False',
        },
      ],
      hints: [
        { ar: 'لا تعدّل البيانات ولا الحلقة — العيب بالكامل داخل valid_story: بادئة بلا مسافة واختبار كلمة I want ضيّع جداً.', en: 'Do not touch the data or the loop — the defect is entirely inside valid_story: a prefix without its trailing space and a too-loose I want substring check.' },
        { ar: 'قارن مع القاعدة الصحيحة: s.startswith(\'As a \') بمسافة، و\', I want \' بالفاصلة، و\', so that \' بالفاصلة — ثلاثة فحوص بـand.', en: "Compare with the correct rule: s.startswith('As a ') with the space, ', I want ' with the comma, ', so that ' with the comma — three checks joined by and." },
        { ar: 'لماذا خدعت القاعدة القديمة؟ لأن ST-4 تبدأ بـAs a وتحوي I want — لكن بلا فاصلة ولا so that: القبول الوهمي صامت لا يرمي استثناء.', en: 'Why did the old rule lie? ST-4 starts with As a and contains I want — but no comma, no so that: the phantom acceptance is silent, it throws nothing.' },
        { ar: 'الإصلاح:\ndef valid_story(s):\n    return s.startswith(\'As a \') and \', I want \' in s and \', so that \' in s\nوبعدها ST-4 Must INVALID والحصيلة stories: 4 valid: 3 must: 2.', en: "The fix:\ndef valid_story(s):\n    return s.startswith('As a ') and ', I want ' in s and ', so that ' in s\nAfterwards ST-4 Must INVALID and the tally stories: 4 valid: 3 must: 2." },
      ],
    },
    {
      kind: 'sandbox',
      starterCode: "STORIES = [\n    {'key': 'ST-1', 'priority': 'Must', 'story': 'As a clerk, I want to flag a patient, so that the clinician prepares.'},\n    {'key': 'ST-2', 'priority': 'Must', 'story': 'As a clinician, I want faster charts.'},\n]\n\ndef valid_story(s):\n    return s.startswith('As a ') and ', I want ' in s and ', so that ' in s\n\nfor st in STORIES:\n    print(st['key'], 'valid' if valid_story(st['story']) else 'INVALID')\n\n# جرّب: أصلح ST-2 بكتابة جملة so that حقيقية — أين ستضيفها في الحزمة؟\n# try: fix ST-2 by writing a real so-that clause — where does it move in the pack?\n# جرّب: خفّض أولوية ST-2 إلى Should — يتغير شيء في valid؟ و في must؟\n# try: demote ST-2 to Should — does valid change? does must?\n# جرّب: أضف حالة إساءة ثالثة وأعطها صنف STRIDE من عندك\n# try: add a third abuse case with a STRIDE category of your own",
      prompt: {
        ar: 'الملعب يربط الفصل كله في حركة واحدة: أكمل فائدة ST-2 وشاهد صعودها من INVALID إلى عدّ must، ثم خفّض أولويتها ولاحظ أي رقم يتحرك وأي ثابت — الصلاحية والأولوية بابان مستقلان. وأخيرًا أضف حالة إساءة بصنف STRIDE من عندك: هكذا تنمو الحزمة من بيانات تمارين إلى أصل مشروع حي. لا اختبار هنا — فضولك فقط.',
        en: 'The sandbox ties the whole chapter in one move: complete ST-2\u2019s benefit and watch it rise from INVALID into the must tally; then demote its priority and notice which number moves and which stays — validity and priority are independent gates. Finally add an abuse case with your own STRIDE tag: that is how the pack grows from exercise data into a living project asset. No tests here — just your curiosity.',
      },
    },
